Z||000000||Madrox86GT||11-09-2000||06:06 PM||||ok everyone i need your help.  i want to install a 10 in my console...i need some drawn up plans if anyone has some...i want to put 6X9's in the doors where the map pockets are but yet work i have water hitting the speaker if it goes through thre door??  wont it go into the door frame and hit the speaker?  any way i need some drawn up plans on how do do that also...<BR>Then....i want to replace the speakers in my seats...so how to do that?  i already have a 8" under the dash where the stock one is located...but i want that 10 also...dont ask about that..and last but not least....can you get q-logic speaker boxes to fix around the kick pannel?  just a thought...<P>please please help me!!!!<P>------------------<BR>You know my saying is:<P>"life is  a  B I T C H... then you marry one."<P>-BLACK 86 GT-  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||11-09-2000||08:09 PM||||An eight inch sub will fit better in the console, in my opinion. Probably can't fit a box in there that has enough volume for a 10" sub (or can you?) Speakers mounted in the doors do run the risk of getting wet. Make sure your dew strips (lower window seals) are in good shape. There are a couple options to help protect the speakers. I like using those waterproof foam baffles that are available from Crutchfield's and most stereo shops. The window riser might run into a 6X9 speaker when you roll the window down. Better measure carefully. To get to the headrest speakers, you must remove the seat back covers. Don't know about the Q-logic. Probably will have to build a custom box for down there. Here is a pic of my former 85 GT. It had an 8" sub in the console.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/GTsubwoofer.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 11-09-2000).]||||reg||1
